# BitTorrent webseed (BEP 19). A multi-file torrent's webseed URL is built as
# <url-list><name>/<path>, so a client fetching this site's torrent asks for
# /tbm/index.html, /tbm/favicon/favicon.ico and so on. The site is served at the
# root, so map that prefix back onto it. 200, not 301: a redirect would work for
# a browser but several clients treat a 3xx on a webseed as a failed range
# request and drop the seed. Nothing else links these paths; robots.txt keeps
# them out of the index so they cannot read as duplicate content.
#
# The splat alone is not enough. Cloudflare Pages runs its own clean-URL
# canonicalisation AFTER a 200 rewrite resolves, so /tbm/index.html rewrites to
# /index.html and Pages then 308s that to / -- the exact 3xx-on-a-webseed this
# rule exists to avoid. Verified 2026-08-13: all 17 HTML paths in the torrent
# returned 308, every non-HTML path returned 200/206. Netlify serves the same
# paths 200, so this is Pages-only.
#
# These rules name each HTML file's ALREADY-CANONICAL target, so there is
# nothing left for Pages to normalise. They must stay above the splat, which
# remains the catch-all for the other 763 files. Regenerate if a page is added:
# the torrent's file list is the source of truth.
/tbm/index.html  /  200
/tbm/404.html  /404  200
/tbm/archive/index.html  /archive/  200
/tbm/art/index.html  /art/  200
/tbm/art/essentialism/index.html  /art/essentialism/  200
/tbm/essentialism/index.html  /essentialism/  200
